+# Pulse (ext-pulse.js)
+
+One sheet with four cards, money first and in plain words. Open it with the **Pulse** button on Today, "Pulse" in All tools, the
+palette ("Pulse", "Money this month", "Close the day"), or the links `#pulse`, `#trading-clock`, `#one-thing`, `#money-month`,
+`#close-the-day`.
+
+- **Trading clock.** Where the New York session is, as a ring and a sentence: before the window, window open before the NY open,
+  the NY session on, no new entries until flat at 15:55, the bots flat for the day, or no session on a weekend. The bots' entry
+  window is 02:00-15:30 ET, the NY open 09:30, flat 15:55 (STRATEGY.md). It counts the time to the next milestone and adds the bots'
+  last live status (a bot in a trade, stopped, eval room thin or how much is left), read only from the device copy `planner.ext.live`
+  that Bots and projects keeps.
+- **Today's one thing.** If you only finish one task today, which? Pick it from up to four suggestions (overdue first, then priority);
+  a big round tick completes it through the Planner's own `snapshot()` + `commit()` (so Undo works) and says the day is a win.
+  Change it any time. Kept on this device only (`planner.pulse.one`, per day).
+- **Money this month.** Income in, costs out and the net so far this month against the same days of last month ("you are $X ahead /
+  behind"), six months of net as bars, the net by project and the three biggest costs. **+ Money in / - Money out** is a two-tap quick
+  add (amount, what for) written to the money log on today's date, the way the money log's own form writes it. A bad amount shows a
+  plain error and adds nothing.
+- **Close the day.** Tasks done and still open, focus minutes, habits checked, money today, the bots' status and your one thing, in a
+  few lines. **Copy** puts them on the clipboard; **Save to my journal** appends them to today's journal entry once (saving twice never
+  duplicates it).
+
+## Notes for the lead (not for the Help sheet)
+- Code: `planner/ext-pulse.js`, loaded by one `<script src="ext-pulse.js">` in `<head>` after ext-board.js. It waits for `planner:ready`
+  and needs `PlannerAPI` (`commit`, `snapshot`, `upsert`, `uid`, `todayKey`, `refreshTasks`, `HB_TOOLS`, `PK_CMDS`).
+- Data: no new synced collection. Money entries and journal text go through the app's own `S.money` / `S.journal` and `commit()`.
+  The only new key is the device key `planner.pulse.one` (`{ day, id }`).
+- Effects: follows the Olympus layer (`--ox-a`, `--ox-b`, `html.ox-move`); no endless animation; reduced motion = none.
+- Pure helpers on `window.__pu`: `sessionClock`, `moneyMonth`, `suggestOne`, `closeLines`, `WIN`, `etNow`.
+- Tests: `planner/tests/pulse.test.js` (PORT env, default 8789; 41 checks).
